# Iconify video operations

Use a real icon as a semantic glyph. Prefer Lucide outlines for a new coherent
set; honor an explicitly supplied provider ID or existing family.

```text
uv run --script <skill-root>/scripts/iconify.py search --query "database" --prefix lucide --limit 6 --out options.json --html options.html
uv run --script <skill-root>/scripts/iconify.py download --id lucide:database --color "#333e48" --size 24 --output database.svg
```

Search and option galleries remain outside the film. The actual chosen SVG and
its receipt are the handoff. Inspect silhouettes and optical weight, not just
names. A complete-set request authorizes a coherent selection; do not add an
unnecessary confirmation step after the requested family is clear.

The helper records provider ID, export dimensions, source/license metadata and
SHA-256. Read and retain the full upstream license text for redistribution.
Keep original multicolor brand assets only when their identity is required;
their source colors are distinct from authored scene paint.

Return a local, script-free SVG with native bounds and a focus port. Use a
consistent stroke and `currentColor` or exact charcoal/red tokens. Strip the
selection gallery's numbering, cards and captions from the film. Preserve a
necessary entity name when the glyph alone is ambiguous.

Mark a monochrome glyph `data-lw-icon="monochrome"`. White is mandatory on a
primary-red face; use dark ink on light gray/white. The bundled theme adapts
inline paths, symbols and external SVG images without removing their holes.
Keep real multicolor brands unmarked with a white backing when needed. Center
the complete icon/label block in both axes, after fonts/assets load. Give each
face its own parent or explicit `data-lw-content` with `data-lw-for="face-id"`.
Use `LineWorldTheme.audit(svg)` to verify contrast, center and containment in
active, inactive and return-seek states. Inspect actual strokes at playback size.

Use [Iconify's official API](https://iconify.design/docs/api/) for source details.
Never replace an unavailable exact requested icon with a fabricated logo.
